{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_087676e90631b7f7e584a10785e506fad53963e64aa14b73af9c0f67d5c57a76","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"eneskirca/nodeterm@8fd38d2c229e snapshot f57e03c407f29b9f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_73f22a3afb1714a42fe4cbf0f42d77d37ccb9fdfccd9dfb721a43d86db9f3532"],"source_ids":["src_a6ed75c969f154ae924b31a6e7e21a32"],"text":"Services (PTY, workspace/settings, git, agents, hooks) live in src/core behind a CorePlatform interface and never import Electron; the browser Server Edition boots the same services over a WebSocket-RPC bridge.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0cd17d9257880fef00d88ec6e0623d2a933ee10f174623a99d5802addfbbbc2b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"eneskirca/nodeterm@8fd38d2c229e snapshot f57e03c407f29b9f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_73f22a3afb1714a42fe4cbf0f42d77d37ccb9fdfccd9dfb721a43d86db9f3532"],"source_ids":["src_a6ed75c969f154ae924b31a6e7e21a32"],"text":"The app is Electron with three contexts: src/main as the shell, src/preload as the sole bridge exposing window.nodeTerminal, and src/renderer as React UI, with src/shared holding types and IPC channel names used by all three.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_25333948595f7f979f919cdc767158311e7056a49176ff63f6d0982ab59dfa91","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"eneskirca/nodeterm@8fd38d2c229e snapshot f57e03c407f29b9f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e2f5c043a86f52ba3d747fce5a5fc9c74597acfaeaf59ce8125096bafe3d1d7b"],"source_ids":["src_a6ed75c969f154ae924b31a6e7e21a32"],"text":"Windows support is beta: the installer is unsigned, updates are manual, and restart-to-restart session continuity is still landing because Windows lacks tmux; a standalone session host replacing it is being packaged.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_36c34b27f25898c9ea153d3d4bc65b66f48916b9dff2036ebc70a7fdd2f1a3d7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"eneskirca/nodeterm@8fd38d2c229e snapshot f57e03c407f29b9f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_738d5c50253e6b94296941b3f50cfd26553458804fa3bc6f2b3c4b3bc84987cf","slc_aa8124a31acb604d1c2c339a5c94839fb59fe7661c390c389d3c7863915b0fb3","slc_f49a61a5efa8b11e2c52c70d7d50121ccc5c941d7421d2b06311d56307252b79"],"source_ids":["src_7382c6b6bb4d5184bdbd1e5c4761ecb1"],"text":"Repository development practice: the process-boundary split is enforced by guard tests that fail if src/core or src/server import electron or ../main/*, and new service logic must go in src/core behind CorePlatform.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3d40a8e748d1b4bf9e6cecd6fe0eacf130542203168c45f8399a21b0f38182e9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"eneskirca/nodeterm@8fd38d2c229e snapshot f57e03c407f29b9f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_15d1d124527d31abfdac8dba5e724feb26280c9cab6a48afaad48a328f7af2b3","slc_60708dbce4bc940a1c76269e6a366eb1e4e5aee5622459d9e3ae7c0cced905d5"],"source_ids":["src_a6ed75c969f154ae924b31a6e7e21a32"],"text":"The project targets people with scattered workflows who want a spatial canvas of terminals and live Claude Code sessions instead of stacked terminal tabs, across desktop, self-hosted browser, and iOS surfaces.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3f898eaa8d37498fe04c0500d3acb5e9bd1268b603d1a4ea416ada4bc7a7d947","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"eneskirca/nodeterm@8fd38d2c229e snapshot f57e03c407f29b9f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8bc97a51f743d8edbabc5ba599076a02aa1ce3c0bbb2055dc38711c55329653c","slc_eb252a7e1f63a7f020cab44bd8efbd4de2b0c8e751002f6551b2a12210f898a0","slc_ff3370ceffa963f9ffff7bfbb2f46769f8fe1921499fcd3fc1445a1513077f3f"],"source_ids":["src_7382c6b6bb4d5184bdbd1e5c4761ecb1","src_a6ed75c969f154ae924b31a6e7e21a32"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors run npm install, npm run dev, npm run typecheck (described as the fastest correctness gate), and npm test (vitest unit + integration); Windows uses bootstrap-windows.bat instead of npm install.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_661d393fc66356c62e7d5a27ac9c1a6eabb725268487c261bcd2b6db718c25ec","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"eneskirca/nodeterm@8fd38d2c229e snapshot f57e03c407f29b9f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_02c66914095aca507c6db0d667231ba866ccdac098ec941cb0752462f25a5fec"],"source_ids":["src_a6ed75c969f154ae924b31a6e7e21a32"],"text":"The Server Edition runs headless on a Linux or macOS host, accessed from any browser with single-user password auth, a WebSocket bridge, and the same renderer as the desktop app.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_737518d05fb0451597e68b750ca1d8e529ab692c5da2529c48ed95fb018cb2b5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"eneskirca/nodeterm@8fd38d2c229e snapshot f57e03c407f29b9f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_52dcf72fa7416cf6f021f232c0250143b68eb9e0c24ce446b2fcfac45f5ed67c"],"source_ids":["src_d7a7afc4463e59e9b823137e963c13ef"],"text":"Bundled components include Electron, React, React Flow, xterm, Monaco, node-pty, zustand, electron-updater/builder, ws, and tweetnacl, plus tmux/libevent/utf8proc in macOS builds; the Anthropic agent SDK is proprietary.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7cff94270b1ed89720011b86265ae6f6a75efd57da92e5e0cf326e1e7ec5b742","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"eneskirca/nodeterm@8fd38d2c229e snapshot f57e03c407f29b9f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_73f22a3afb1714a42fe4cbf0f42d77d37ccb9fdfccd9dfb721a43d86db9f3532"],"source_ids":["src_a6ed75c969f154ae924b31a6e7e21a32"],"text":"The renderer depends only on a TerminalTransport abstraction: LocalTransport talks to the local host and RemoteTransport to a remote agent over SSH, so remote projects drop in without canvas UI changes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7e02a8c44ce62f8ec6d42e2c852f68e49a5e16fb11272a16e82e0dfefaaf78a8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"eneskirca/nodeterm@8fd38d2c229e snapshot f57e03c407f29b9f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_be9474040cca0c842b2c775f45e3e5ef0f2b577fc5352479f6f9bb88a61177ca","slc_d69f6a6862bb9ec2705152f2a83372283431a61b426fcc2fa963fc96441fe275"],"source_ids":["src_a6ed75c969f154ae924b31a6e7e21a32","src_d7a7afc4463e59e9b823137e963c13ef"],"text":"Terminals run in persistent tmux sessions surviving node remounts, app restarts, and machine reboots, restoring scrollback and resuming agent sessions via claude --resume; the macOS app bundles its own tmux, preferring any system tmux.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_897141901f4d7d443af844eafbad34eac0a0b294dcf626b3cb507b0b77601353","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"eneskirca/nodeterm@8fd38d2c229e snapshot f57e03c407f29b9f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_59be09c210c7ae3e72512cc28b9bbf00e2aa4a543c33dbf4c232db8a2328d693","slc_ba876b872841716ea8df53cf047a67ea20657567eac503d5d976a2d9f4bd1658","slc_e166f7fc3ef1d9e2d89a395c180885413fffe19e8bc03f118377e9b5160c345d"],"source_ids":["src_7382c6b6bb4d5184bdbd1e5c4761ecb1"],"text":"Repository development practice: house rules require atomic file writes via renameAtomic/writeFileAtomic, an 'error' listener on child stdin before the first write, and credentials never passed on argv, each backed by guard tests that fail PRs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","created_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_be7cc3e4fd93465e3cfa218f813650761bd9956dd5d486ea8c43f4afbbe2227c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"eneskirca/nodeterm@8fd38d2c229e snapshot f57e03c407f29b9f","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ff57bc0518f82445872e07cfe4c17bd04d38c8d4640e65fb66251824567f4932"],"source_ids":["src_a6ed75c969f154ae924b31a6e7e21a32"],"text":"Node kinds include terminal (xterm + tmux), agent (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, Copilot, opencode, Grok, custom), sticky notes linkable as agent context, groups bound to git worktrees, Monaco editors, diff views, and web/video nodes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:48:25Z","updated_by_operation":"op_ec7d69edafab4e24a476a6e6e73b17a7"}
